# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Regaal 8
family Borstwerk
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.008 s 15 dB 3 14
# Borstwerk: a short-resonator reed, buzzy, its upper harmonics strong.
harmonics 1 0.6  2 0.7  3 0.8  4 0.75  5 0.7  6 0.65  7 0.6  8 0.55
harmonics 9 0.5  10 0.45  11 0.4  12 0.35  13 0.3  14 0.27  15 0.24  16 0.2  18 0.15  20 0.1
level 2 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
